<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Research AI Café #002 | EN"><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><div class="eyebrow">Research AI Café #002 | EN</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.7rem)">How are you using AI<br/>in your research?</h1><p class="lead">An English-language roundtable on real AI practices among experimental researchers.</p><a class="event-poster" href="/images/research-ai-cafe-002-en-poster.webp" aria-label="Open the English poster at full size"><img src="/images/research-ai-cafe-002-en-poster.webp" alt="Research AI Café #002 English poster. The theme is How are you using AI in your research? Date, venue, and registration details are TBD." width="900" height="1274" /></a><div class="card event-facts"><strong>Date</strong><p>TBD</p><strong>Venue</strong><p>TBD</p><strong>Who</strong><p>Graduate students and early-career researchers, especially in experimental fields; all disciplines are welcome.</p><strong>Language</strong><p>English</p><strong>Fee</strong><p>Free</p></div><h2>Questions for this session</h2><ul><li>Where do you use AI in research?</li><li>What has been genuinely useful?</li><li>What has felt unsafe or unreliable?</li><li>How do practices differ across fields or research cultures?</li><li>What would you like to try next?</li></ul><h2>Planned format</h2><ul><li>Opening</li><li>Snapshot of current use</li><li>Lightning talk</li><li>Group discussion</li><li>Whole-group reflection</li><li>Informal conversation</li></ul><h2>Registration</h2><p>The registration form is being prepared.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
